{
  "id": "KP09Z",
  "version": "2.0",
  "title": "Non-surgical arm fracture treatment",
  "description": "Non-surgical arm fracture treatment is an outpatient procedure where your doctor treats your broken arm without surgery by immobilizing it with a cast or sling. Your doctor will take X-rays to determine the type and severity of your fracture. If the break is stable and properly aligned, surgery is typically not needed. Your doctor will apply a cast or sling to immobilize your arm so the bone can heal. You'll need to keep your arm still and avoid strenuous activities for several weeks. X-rays will be taken periodically to monitor healing. Once the cast is removed, physical therapy helps restore your strength and motion. Some fractures may need the bones manipulated into proper position before casting. The cost of this procedure may vary depending on whether your doctor needs to manually reposition (manipulate) the bone fragments into proper alignment, or whether the fracture can heal in its current position without manipulation.",
